          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 06:41:19.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 123ac and 123ad",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 123ac and 123ad\n\nPass 2 of sanity 123ac ran \"statx --cached=always -D\", which\nonly lists names and never calls statx(). It always timed as\n0 seconds, so its loop never stopped early, and every run\ncreated and unlinked 100000 files without checking anything:\nabout 540 seconds of 620. Add -l so that the pass really does\nstat each file, which gives AT_STATX_DONT_SYNC its first test,\nand cap it at 1000 files.\n\nMost of 123ad went on running the base test twice, for a speed\ncheck that only logs in a VM. Drop those runs and use one set\nof files for both statahead settings. The hit count and RPC\nchecks are unchanged.\n\nQuote the format in pass 1 of 123ac, so that its fields are no\nlonger passed as file names, and print the batched RPC count,\nwhich was always empty.\n\nWith the CI debug mask on one ldiskfs node, 123ac goes from\n640 to 44 seconds and 123ad from 309 to 58 seconds.\n\nFixes: 3f7853b31ef6 (\"LU-10934 llite: integrate statx() API with Lustre\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123ac 123ad\"\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123ac 123ad\" fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123ac 123ad\" mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123ac 123ad\" clientarch=aarch64 clientdistro=rocky9.8\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123ac 123ad\" clientdistro=ubuntu2404\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ida0e6efc52f8019a717c1ae1e990317fce16e665\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70342\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
